Package: coldspot
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: asuramaya <asuramaya@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), systemd, openssh-client, nftables
Recommends: clang, bpftool, linux-tools-common, network-manager
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/asuramaya/coldspot
Description: metered-link data saver — per-app truth, hard caps, GNOME pill
 coldspot governs a metered or unreliable link: an eBPF-backed daemon meters
 every app's bytes, a CAKE-shaped cap protects the budget while priority
 protects the task you're actively running, and a GNOME Quick Settings pill
 shows live per-app rates with tap-to-cap/uncap/block. Link-health sensing
 (signal, PHY rate, loss) drives auto-stabilize and health-gated multi-radio
 steering/bonding. Pure Python standard library core; no pip dependencies.
